          "extra_snippets": [
            "FriskAI wants to close that gap, and it has raised $3.6 million in pre-seed funding to build the tooling to do so. MaC Venture Capital, which has backed companies including Pipe, Blavity and IronVest, led the round, joined by Wischoff Ventures, NEA partner Rick Yang and a group of strategic angel investors.",
            "The $3.6 million in FriskAI’s total funding to date will go toward expanding its engineering and go-to-market teams.",
            "FriskAI is a small player in a field that’s filling up fast. Manifold raised $8 million to secure agents at the endpoint. Geordie AI closed a $30 million Series A for agent governance. NeuralTrust, which TFN covered when it announced what it calls Europe’s largest cybersecurity seed round, raised $20 million for a similar control layer.",
            "Jason Moore, a staff software engineer at Sana Benefits, is already using it. “FriskAI gives us the operational visibility we’ve been missing, helping us troubleshoot issues faster and deploy AI with confidence instead of guesswork,” he said."
          ]
